        "username": "skywhale",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/skywhale/{size}/5248_2.png",
        "created_at": "2022-06-23T16:36:00.118Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Trajector\" data-post=\"22\" data-topic=\"29363\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/48/1914_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Trajector:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>So anyway, during a full Moon, the Earth and everyone on it are located right between the Sun, a source of energy, and the Moon, a mirror. So werewolves must be a lasing medium, and the rest of humans aren’t.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Not to question your highly accurate Werewolf science, but what is the partially reflective mirror in this scenario? And what is the “beam” that is being projected?</p>\n<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/original/2X/d/d99f6cf3839058aa1dfc367e570033b868557694.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/d99f6cf3839058aa1dfc367e570033b868557694\" title=\"image\"><img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/d/d99f6cf3839058aa1dfc367e570033b868557694_2_517x271.jpeg\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"v3bb5sE8uAY6XkcpwVRz9aeOy0Y\" width=\"517\" height=\"271\" srcset=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/d/d99f6cf3839058aa1dfc367e570033b868557694_2_517x271.jpeg, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/d/d99f6cf3839058aa1dfc367e570033b868557694_2_775x406.jpeg 1.5x, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/d/d99f6cf3839058aa1dfc367e570033b868557694_2_1034x542.jpeg 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"3B3B46\"><div class=\"meta\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">image</span><span class=\"informations\">1640×861 65.4 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg></div></a></div></p>",
