      {
        "id": 249593,
        "name": "",
        "username": "The_Justifier",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_justifier/{size}/4954_2.png",
        "created_at": "2022-11-25T17:01:24.885Z",
        "cooked": "<p>A lot to say on this episode as well, now that I’m caught up to it.  I think a lot about, for lack of a better term, the science of supernatural creatures; it’s acceptable that C&amp;A are loose with this kind of lore, since comics only try so hard to make sense or be realistic, but I do like to try and Justify things a little more.</p>\n<p>From a scientific perspective, the problem with a large number of vampires is that, especially with much of the sun’s light being blocked out, the vampire population will rapidly deplete the accessible sources of useful energy.  Plants would no longer grow, and anything not in a seed vault would be permanently extinct even if the cloud eventually cleared.  Vampires would rapidly run out of people, animals, plants cultured to produce blood, combustible fuels to operate steampunk devices, and any electrical supply not tied to a geothermal or hydrodynamic stationary location.  Technology would not be able to save the vampires for long, and most fictional magic systems come with some sort of cost for power, so it’s likely this couldn’t fix the problem either.</p>",
        "post_number": 32,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2022-11-25T18:42:25.028Z",
